From 5f1321879f348f5c636f9b208ee816b29241b6a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:18:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: t8152-aop-audio: require verified pw0 before
 rearming sense ring

Do not clear spkr running state or stop SenseRing DMA when a pw0
transition fails in spkr_stop_locked() (except on shutdown, which still
releases DMA resources while keeping running set). On suspend, still
stop and synchronize SenseRing DMA and record resume_run even when pw0
fails, because snd_soc_component_suspend() discards the callback error
and proceeds with sleep.

Track pw0_verified in SpkrState, clear it before every pwrd attempt so
an unconfirmed pwrd failure forces a fresh verified pw0 before rearming,
have resume_with_ring() verify pw0 via ensure_pw0() when running or
unverified before rearming SenseRing, and fail closed in both
resume_with_ring() and start_with_ring() if pw0 still fails so neither
prepare nor resume can arm RX on a running or unverified serializer.

Add KUnit coverage in spkr_state_requires_verified_pw0_before_rearm and
spkr_state_suspend_pw0_failure_and_resume.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
---
 sound/soc/apple/t8152_aop_audio.rs | 566 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 511 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/t8152_aop_audio.rs b/sound/soc/apple/t8152_aop_audio.rs
